{
  "$type": "shadow",
  "$description": "The site's shadow recipes, stored as layers because that is Penpot's own shape — offsetX / offsetY / blur / spread / color, with 8-digit hex so the alpha travels. panel/popup/chip are two-layer (tight contact plus wide soft); `panel` lifts the mega-menu; `popup` is the same recipe scaled down for the place-map popup and tooltips; `chip` is smaller again, for inline code and the webmention avatars. `thumb` is Tobias Ahlin's five equal layers (1–16px) for images and covers lying on the page, tinted blue-gray in light; `thumb-cast` is the same five layers for an object lit from the top left, falling right by half the drop and stronger in light (the pamphlet; its dark twin equals thumb-dark); picked in _local/design/Reference - Shadow lab. All go deeper on dark. tailwind.config.js composes the layers into --box-shadow-*; build-penpot-tokens.js emits each into theme/light and its -dark twin into theme/dark under the same name.",
